# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000085  -  CAT II
# The web server must have Web Distributed Authoring (WebDAV) disabled.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000085
group:           V-206383
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise ships no Web Distributed Authoring service, so there is
                 no WebDAV module to disable; the application's share is that the
                 remote-authoring behavior it does have - endpoints that change state
                 through an HTTP GET - is switched off.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] enable_insecure_pdfgen in false|0
check:           web.conf [settings] enable_secure_entity_move in true|1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enable_insecure_login https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] enable_insecure_login in false|0
                 reason: "Whether or not the GET-based '/account/insecurelogin' REST
                         endpoint is enabled. Provides an alternate GET-based authentication
                         mechanism. If 'true', the following url is available:
                         http://localhost:8000/en-US/account/insecurelogin?loginType=splunk&username=noc&password=XXXXXXX.
                         If 'false', only the main /account/login endpoint is available.
                         Default: false"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        WebDAV offered by any separate web server or module placed in front of the
                 application, carried by that component and the operating system.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000085 check and fix text;
                 web.conf.spec:198 (enable_insecure_login, default false),
                 web.conf.spec:221 (enable_insecure_pdfgen, default false),
                 web.conf.spec:206 (enable_secure_entity_move, default true)
finding:         One of Splunk Web's GET-based state-changing endpoints is enabled, so the
                 application exposes remote authoring through a URL even though it ships no
                 WebDAV service.
